# The settings of scripts/security-signals.sh, Heimdall's security signal job, for one environment. Copy to
# $YGG_SECRETS_DIR/security-signals-<environment>.env (default /etc/yggdrasil/security-signals-production.env;
# `ygg install` does it for production), chmod 600, owned by ygg, and fill in. Never commit the copy.
#
# Each line is read literally: NAME=value, no quotes, no `export`, no comments after a value (put them on lines of
# their own, as here). It is not shell.

# The plain key of Hermes's `heimdall-signals` client in this environment. Hermes keeps only its hash. Never the key
# of the API's own Hermes client: that one shares Heimdall's limits, and the flood that raises a signal could use
# them up.
HEIMDALL_SIGNAL_HERMES_API_KEY=

# Where the alerts go: the one address on the `fixed` recipient list of that client. Any other is answered 403.
HEIMDALL_SIGNAL_ALERT_TO=

# The ping URL of a heartbeat monitor that takes the exit status as the last path segment and mails its owner when a
# ping reports a failure or stops arriving: https://hc-ping.com/<uuid> on healthchecks.io, for example. Create the
# check with a period of 15 minutes and a grace time of 15 minutes. Without this a failed run reaches nobody, and the
# clocks of the LGPD and the GDPR run from awareness. Nothing but the exit status is ever sent to it.
HEIMDALL_SIGNAL_HEARTBEAT_URL=
